## Acceptance Criteria

### AC-1: Data Completeness

- [ ] All source rows matching filter criteria are present in target
- [ ] Row count differential between source and target is < {{ threshold | default("0.1%") }}
- [ ] No orphaned records in target after full refresh

### AC-2: Transformation Correctness

- [ ] Business rules produce expected output for sample inputs
- [ ] NULL handling follows documented behavior for each field
- [ ] Data types in target match schema definition

### AC-3: Timeliness

- [ ] Pipeline completes within SLA window
- [ ] Late-arriving data is handled per documented edge case behavior
- [ ] Monitoring/alerting is in place for SLA breaches

### AC-4: Idempotency

- [ ] Running the pipeline twice produces the same result
- [ ] No duplicate rows after re-execution

---

## Edge Cases

| Scenario | Expected Behavior |
|----------|-------------------|
| Source table is empty | Target remains unchanged; log warning |
| Source has duplicate keys | Deduplicate using latest timestamp |
| Schema drift (new column in source) | Ignore unknown columns; log for review |
| Target table doesn't exist | Create it from DDL artifact |
| Network timeout during load | Retry up to 3 times with backoff |

